# Rules that split a complex into three products.
#
# "+" between product patterns says the molecules in them end up in different
# complexes, all of them: a rule with three products may fire only if no two
# of the three are still connected once its bonds are deleted. Testing the two
# molecules of each deleted bond is not enough. Two products that the rule
# never bonded to each other can still be bonded to each other somewhere else.
#
# The model has two families, each present as 100 chains and 100 rings.
#
# SplitBonds deletes the two bonds of A, to B and to C, and writes
# "A + B + C". On a chain B-A-C the three come apart, so it fires and Chain3
# falls to 0. On a ring B and C are also bonded to each other, so they stay in
# one complex and it must never fire: Ring3 stays at 100.
#
# SplitDeleted deletes X and Y, which hold D to E and D to F, and writes
# "D + E + F". On a chain E-X-D-Y-F the three come apart, so it fires and
# Chain5 falls to 0. On a ring E and F are also bonded to each other, so it
# must never fire: Ring5 stays at 100.
#
# BioNetGen's network generator agrees. Given this model it produces two
# reactions, SplitBonds on the chain and SplitDeleted on the chain.
#
# NFsim tested only the molecules at the two ends of each deleted bond (A and
# B, A and C) and the molecules each deleted molecule held (D and E, D and F),
# so both rules broke every ring as well.

begin model
begin parameters
  k  1.0
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b,c)
  B(a,c)
  C(a,b)
  D(x,y)
  X(d,e)
  Y(d,f)
  E(x,f)
  F(y,e)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1,c).C(a!2,b)                                   100
  A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1,c!3).C(a!2,b!3)                               100
  D(x!1,y!2).X(d!1,e!3).E(x!3,f).Y(d!2,f!4).F(y!4,e)             100
  D(x!1,y!2).X(d!1,e!3).E(x!3,f!5).Y(d!2,f!4).F(y!4,e!5)         100
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules  Chain3  A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1,c).C(a!2,b)
  Molecules  Ring3   A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1,c!3).C(a!2,b!3)
  Molecules  Chain5  D(x!1,y!2).X(d!1,e!3).E(x!3,f).Y(d!2,f!4).F(y!4,e)
  Molecules  Ring5   D(x!1,y!2).X(d!1,e!3).E(x!3,f!5).Y(d!2,f!4).F(y!4,e!5)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  SplitBonds:   A(b!1,c!2).B(a!1).C(a!2) -> A(b,c) + B(a) + C(a)   k
  SplitDeleted: D(x!1,y!2).X(d!1,e!3).E(x!3).Y(d!2,f!4).F(y!4) -> D(x,y) + E(x) + F(y)   k  DeleteMolecules
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
